WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.6 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Decision rights and delegation of authority

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Write down who can approve what, up to which limit, before you open a bank account or sign a contract.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
A delegation of authority states who may approve what, up to which limit: spending, contracts, hiring, partnerships, public statements and access to personal data. The level rises with the risk.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
A ladder that rises with risk

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:37.500
One founder: Small purchases within the budget and daily delivery choices, with receipts kept. For example: A bakery founder buys flour and paper bags within the monthly budget.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:48.830
All co-founders: Larger purchases, first hires, contracts and partner agreements, with a second signatory. For example: Both bakery founders sign the order for a new oven after getting two quotes.

7
00:00:48.830 --> 00:01:00.530
Governing body: Reserved matters: budget, strategy, major contracts, borrowing and key policies, recorded in minutes. For example: Once registered, the bakery's board approves a loan to fit out its own shop.

8
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:12.319
Members or shareholders: Changing the founding document, electing the board and sharing any surplus. For example: The founders, as shareholders, vote to reinvest the year's profit in the bakery.

9
00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:13.319
Why it matters

10
00:01:13.319 --> 00:01:19.363
1. It saves arguments before you open a bank account or sign contracts.

11
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:25.778
2. A second check protects you from mistakes, even if you are only two.

12
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:32.081
3. Partners and funders see that money and promises are controlled.

13
00:01:32.481 --> 00:01:33.081
What it guides

14
00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:38.385
1. Your finance procedures in Module 9, with the same thresholds.

15
00:01:38.385 --> 00:01:43.319
2. Your bank mandate: who signs, and above which amount.

16
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:49.993
3. Your role cards: each role's spending limits and when to escalate.

17
00:01:50.393 --> 00:01:50.993
What to avoid

18
00:01:50.993 --> 00:01:57.407
No cover for absence: name who approves when the usual approver is away.

19
00:01:57.407 --> 00:02:03.452
Anyone approving a payment to themselves, or where they have an interest.

20
00:02:03.452 --> 00:02:10.496
Delegating and walking away: whoever delegates still checks how authority is used.

21
00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.896
You draft your first delegation matrix with absence and conflict rules.

22
00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:16.896
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:18.396 --> 00:02:21.496
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
